{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new functions and refactors existing ones to improve usability and consistency. It also updates type checking logic and removes legacy Python 2 support.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The public API must expose the `apply` function, which accepts a callable and arguments to invoke it. The library must also provide `identity` and `thread_first` as part of its standard interface."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The release must include the `compose_left` function for left-to-right composition of callables. Additionally, `compose` and `pipe` must be available for functional composition and piping operations respectively."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "The `peekn` function must be exposed, allowing inspection of multiple items from an iterator without consuming them. The existing `peek` function should remain available for inspecting a single item."
    },
    {
      "id": "m07",
      "text": "The `fold` function must support parallel execution capabilities while maintaining its standard reduction behavior. Its signature and output format should remain consistent with previous versions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "The library's internal breakpoint handling or debugging signals must adhere to updated signatures compatible with modern Python environments. No specific public name changes are required for this adjustment."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14",
      "text": "The `merge` and `merge_with` functions must accept any object implementing the `Mapping` abstract base class, not just standard dictionaries. This allows broader compatibility with custom mapping types."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "All listed functions including `Compose`, `curry`, `excepts`, `get_exclude_keywords`, `groupby`, `has_keywords`, `has_varargs`, `is_partial_args`, `is_valid_args`, `itemfilter`, `itemmap`, `join`, `keyfilter`, `keymap`, `merge_with`, `num_pos_args`, `num_required_args`, `signature_or_spec`, `valfilter`, and `valmap` must operate exclusively on Python 3 syntax and features. Any Python 2 specific code paths or compatibility shims must be removed."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31",
      "text": "The `get_config_from_root` function must emit improved warning messages when configuration issues are detected. These warnings should clearly indicate the nature of the configuration problem."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names are correctly exported and documented. Verify that the removal of Python 2 support does not break existing Python 3 users."
}
